{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095684-roleplaying-raising-gnosis","id":1095684,"title":"Roleplaying: Raising Gnosis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-22T17:51:34-07:00","id":1095684,"title":"Roleplaying: Raising Gnosis","content":"Crowdsourcing y'all: My players and I have just concluded our latest chronicle, and I'll be providing some 'down time' - side quests, character spotlights, and opportunities to explore the strangeness of the setting (Manila) - before we continue on to the next arc. I'm also raising the Gnosis cap from 3 to 4 as well. Any suggestions on how to make this happen organically? How have you played out raising Gnosis in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T17:58:28-07:00","id":1095688,"title":"","content":"A vision quest in reenactment of the Awakening, but this time in the Fallen World, seems like a good thing to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T00:03:34-07:00","id":1095779,"title":"","content":"I just let players spend EXP on Gnosis - basing that they all the time crack 'Mysteries of Universes' - i.e. Mysteries - it does not seems weird their <b><i>Gnosis</i></b> deepen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T00:29:15-07:00","id":1095786,"title":"","content":"I always go with a question:<br /> Do you think that this Mystery was sufficiently enlightening to raise your Gnosis to 4?<br /> Did you do something that could justify rising you Strength?<br /> Do you feel that your character should be represented by Presence X?<br /> Do you think that this new Status dot represent your standing with the x and/or you are ready to change how your character is perceived? Did they do something?<br /> <br /> It's not meant to discourage a player or to take from him possibility to rise his dots but its important to remember that they represent your character in many ways. If you want to take athletics on 5th dot you must know that this means training 8h a day and eating like an elephant. It also changes description of your character, most likely your friends will expand to elite athletes.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to Gnosis its about being aware and 'enlightened' (not necessarily in a Buddhist or Christian way) - just make sure that it fits character in some way and does player really want it and feel like they have a reason to.<br /> It can be rised by cracking a lot of small Mysteries sure, but isn't it more fitting to go for a pilgrimage to a 106 acre Pando forest that is composed from a single organism and possess it to become one with it and spread yourself so thinly? Summon the supernal and let it show you secrets, make it dangerous. Gaining Gnosis is a critical point, talk with a player if he has some idea what would be the most fitting way for his character to rise it, collaborate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-23-2017, 05:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T01:52:53-07:00","id":1095803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095684-roleplaying-raising-gnosis?p=1095688#post1095688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vision quest in reenactment of the Awakening, but this time in the Fallen World, seems like a good thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the recommendation for achieving Archmastery, or binding to an Abyssal Zigurrat, I think it might be a bit much for raising Gnosis (unless you're trying to run a version of the setting where high Gnosis is rarer)<br /> <br /> OP, M2E Has this to say:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the narrative, Gnosis requires knowledge and understanding. It requires moments of epiphany, study, and experience. Gnosis increases when your character has advanced philosophically, mystically, or academically in such a significant way that she\u2019ll never see the world the same. <br /> <br /> While they\u2019re not as influential and life-changing as the Awakening itself, these are moments the character will likely never forget, milestones in her advancement that show clear evolution of thinking, purpose, or identity. </div> </div> </div>Normally, I require pretty major personal 'revelation' decided on by the player. Frequently accompanied by a change in Virtue/Vice, and almost always a new Obsession.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T02:41:19-07:00","id":1095809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095684-roleplaying-raising-gnosis?p=1095803#post1095803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the recommendation for achieving Archmastery, or binding to an Abyssal Zigurrat, I think it might be a bit much for raising Gnosis (unless you're trying to run a version of the setting where high Gnosis is rarer)<br /> <br /> OP, M2E Has this to say:<br /> <br /> <br /> Normally, I require pretty major personal 'revelation' decided on by the player. Frequently accompanied by a change in Virtue/Vice, and almost always a new Obsession.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant to say was along the lines of what you quoted, so that the mage will &quot;never see the world the same.&quot; But yeah, another Awakening is usually too much :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T04:24:32-07:00","id":1095831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1095684-roleplaying-raising-gnosis?p=1095809#post1095809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant to say was along the lines of what you quoted, so that the mage will &quot;never see the world the same.&quot; But yeah, another Awakening is usually too much :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, then yes, I agree with your take for most of the games I've run, and the ones I've played in treat it similarly.<br /> <br /> Wyrd's 'just spend xp' also has its place in a certain kind of game, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T09:37:34-07:00","id":1096388,"title":"","content":"Usually, I require one of two things: Either some grand, significant moment that sparks a Zen kind of instantaneous revelation, or sufficient time off-screen to allow a slower boil of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> A rise in Gnosis is, to my mind, associated with a deepening of internalization of the Mage's Path perspective and all that such entails. As such, it should probably come after the Mage does something appropriate to their Path (or Legacy, or even Order). A Thyrsus rectifies some disturbance in the Shadow; a Mastigos violently lobotomizes a long-time rival with magic; an Obrimos leads their congregation such that their fear abates and stops feeding a monstrous spirit, etc. Summoning a Supernal entity for tutelage is always justification too.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, have it off-screen, representing a great deal of time spent enhancing the Mage's connection to their Path. Spending time exploring their Path in the Astral, communing with spirits, studying ancient texts, etc.<br /> <br /> Justifying a rise in Gnosis shouldn't be difficult if you're willing to allow it. If you can't justify it on-screen, just say it happened off-screen over the course of downtime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}